# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# caches
.turbo/
.cache/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.tgz

# Windows shell cruft (this repo is developed on Windows)
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# macOS resource forks, for anyone cloning on a Mac
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride

# editors / IDEs
# Keep shared workspace config committable, ignore everything personal.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# agent tooling
# Local, per-developer overrides — must not be committed. (Previously this was
# only covered by a user-level global ignore, so a fresh clone would have
# committed it.)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Prisma's agent skills, installed by `npx prisma init` (~0.5 MB of vendor docs
# under .claude/skills, plus .agents/ and .windsurf/ copies it also creates).
# Not committed because:
#   1. They are regenerable — `npx prisma init` lays them down again.
#   2. Its .claude/skills and .windsurf/skills are ABSOLUTE symlinks into
#      .agents/skills. With core.symlinks=false (the Windows default) git commits
#      those as text files containing "/c/Nikhil@pbn/pbn-proposal/...", which
#      resolves to nothing on another machine, in CI, or after moving this folder.
# .agents/ and .windsurf/ have been deleted from this repo; the rules stay so a
# future `prisma init` doesn't quietly stage them again.
# Shared, hand-written .claude config (settings.json, commands, project skills)
# is deliberately NOT covered and stays committable.
/.agents/
/.windsurf/
/.claude/skills/
/skills-lock.json

# debug / logs
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# prisma
# The client is generated from prisma/schema.prisma on postinstall, so it is
# build output rather than source.
/src/generated/prisma/
#
# Do NOT ignore prisma/migrations/ — migration history is source of truth for
# the database and has to be committed and deployed.
